(325985, 24204, 8911, '<td valign="top">I like this. You had a real challenge going for you with the focus, which others have noted. A chair, table, or rail to steady your elbows on might have helped, if movement during the shot was the problem (happens to me a lot with my camera, I fear).<br/> <br/>You might also try the shot again, with the curtain on the window as your right edge - and not the last inch of it, either. It will cut off part of your subject but I suspect it would address the glare.<br/> <br/>The oh-so-serious sign is hysterical next to the whimsy of the toy behind it!</td>', 'I like this. You had a real challenge going for you with the focus, which others have noted. A chair, table, or rail to steady your elbows on might have helped, if movement during the shot was the problem (happens to me a lot with my camera, I fear). You might also try the shot again, with the curtain on the window as your right edge - and not the last inch of it, either. It will cut off part of your subject but I suspect it would address the glare. The oh-so-serious sign is hysterical next to the whimsy of the toy behind it!', '2003-06-16 01:09:27.000000', NULL, 0),
