(325991, 24125, 1143, '<td valign="top">Oops. Didn''t have time to put in any comments before the challenge so here they are:<br/>I don''t work at an office or even have a home office so this challenge wasn''t an easy one. I happened to be cleaning the attic that week and started running into all these antique office tools which gave me the idea to put them all together. <br/>The "desk" is the vanity from a bedroom suite purchased by my grandparents just before he went to the war. He served on a destroyer in the Pacific, and my grandmother saved the paper. The picture is of her brother who also served in WWII. <br/>The tape dispenser came from my grandfather''s desk and is very old although I''m not sure how old. Apparently transparent tape came into use in the 30s. The lamp and phone are two old garage sale finds that both work, and the fan is a reproduction of a 1940s fan. <br/>It''s kind of like a "where''s waldo" picture I guess in that everyone wanted to find something that doesn''t fit. I''m just glad to see people spent that much time looking at it!</td>', 'Oops. Didn''t have time to put in any comments before the challenge so here they are:I don''t work at an office or even have a home office so this challenge wasn''t an easy one. I happened to be cleaning the attic that week and started running into all these antique office tools which gave me the idea to put them all together. The "desk" is the vanity from a bedroom suite purchased by my grandparents just before he went to the war. He served on a destroyer in the Pacific, and my grandmother saved the paper. The picture is of her brother who also served in WWII. The tape dispenser came from my grandfather''s desk and is very old although I''m not sure how old. Apparently transparent tape came into use in the 30s. The lamp and phone are two old garage sale finds that both work, and the fan is a reproduction of a 1940s fan. It''s kind of like a "where''s waldo" picture I guess in that everyone wanted to find something that doesn''t fit. I''m just glad to see people spent that much time looking at it!', '2003-06-16 01:10:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(325993, 24264, 4285, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by orussell:</b></div><hr/><i>I like this one alot. It was my favorite. Man that''s some super macro action you going on there. Superb DOF. The B &amp; W only adds to it. I''m going to go out on a limb here and say that this was probably shot with a Canon EOS-10D. Close? I even think I might know who shot this. Great work. <br/>7</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Guess I was off on this one. Still my top pick.</td>', 'Originally posted by orussell:I like this one alot. It was my favorite. Man that''s some super macro action you going on there. Superb DOF. The B & W only adds to it. I''m going to go out on a limb here and say that this was probably shot with a Canon EOS-10D. Close? I even think I might know who shot this. Great work. 7  Guess I was off on this one. Still my top pick.', '2003-06-16 01:11:21.000000', NULL, 0),
