(326413, 24187, 6900, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the great comments everyone.  I wanted to BE bod-like.  :)  I guess my score didn''t realize it was supposed to hit 6.  I thought this was a much better shot than anyone else thought it was.  And whoever gave me a 1, that''s grand. lol<br/> <br/>Almost hit a 6 and beat my guesstimate by .2, so I''ll take it.  Back to the drawing bod.</td>', 'Thanks for the great comments everyone.  I wanted to BE bod-like.  :)  I guess my score didn''t realize it was supposed to hit 6.  I thought this was a much better shot than anyone else thought it was.  And whoever gave me a 1, that''s grand. lol Almost hit a 6 and beat my guesstimate by .2, so I''ll take it.  Back to the drawing bod.', '2003-06-16 11:02:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(326456, 24102, 656, '<td valign="top">Well deserved winner - congratulations!</td>', 'Well deserved winner - congratulations!', '2003-06-16 11:24:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(326477, 24220, 3087, '<td valign="top"><b>Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/> <br/><b>Initial thoughts</b> <br/>Really like the concept  very subtle and thought-provoking. <br/> <br/><b>Composition/ Content</b> <br/>The concept itself is a clever one  and I particularly like how the image itself doesnt tell us whether you are saying that change is good, bad, inevitable or perhaps none of the above. All it shows us is that many changes have happened in our life times, some major and some minor.<br/>In terms of the image itself, I like the angle of the viewpoint as well as the diagonal of the ipaq within the frame. Its nice that the diagonal is set against the (almost) horizontal and vertical lines of the reflected calendar.<br/>In my opinion the reflection could be a little brighter, though really not much, because the fact its less clear than the ipaq supports the idea that its a ghost from the past.<br/>Lighting on the ipaq seems uneven with a lot more around the navigation buttons than elsewhere.<br/> <br/><b>Background</b> <br/>Clean, rich, appropriate.<br/> <br/><b>Fits The Challenge</b> <br/>Definitely.<br/> <br/><b>My Opinion On The Photo</b> <br/>I like the concept and the thoughts this image provokes better than I like the image visually.</td>', 'Critique Club   Initial thoughts Really like the concept  very subtle and thought-provoking.  Composition/ Content The concept itself is a clever one  and I particularly like how the image itself doesnt tell us whether you are saying that change is good, bad, inevitable or perhaps none of the above. All it shows us is that many changes have happened in our life times, some major and some minor.In terms of the image itself, I like the angle of the viewpoint as well as the diagonal of the ipaq within the frame. Its nice that the diagonal is set against the (almost) horizontal and vertical lines of the reflected calendar.In my opinion the reflection could be a little brighter, though really not much, because the fact its less clear than the ipaq supports the idea that its a ghost from the past.Lighting on the ipaq seems uneven with a lot more around the navigation buttons than elsewhere. Background Clean, rich, appropriate. Fits The Challenge Definitely. My Opinion On The Photo I like the concept and the thoughts this image provokes better than I like the image visually.', '2003-06-16 11:41:08.000000', NULL, 0),
